The tools page reads like the other editions'
==============================================

Core shipped the old skills section: one flat list with a search box, sitting under a wall of connection
cards, with no way to tell the build's own skills from the agent's library on this machine.

What it has now:

  * skills first, connections after — the page is called "Tools & skills" and the instructions are what
    a person opens it for;
  * two libraries, each with its own search, its area chips and a counter: what this build ships, and
    the Hermes library discovered from the profiles on this machine;
  * the whole-page search across connections, tools and skills, with every write conditional so typing
    cannot re-fire the observer on its own output and wedge the page.

The panels group on the engine's `owner`, and the engine now reports it: a skill the manifest names is
`quixidesk`, one found in the user's own directory is `user`, and one found by walking a mounted Hermes
root is `hermes`. That last one is the bug this fixes — the page used to infer provenance from a slash in
the skill id, and a Hermes skill sitting at the TOP of a root has no slash, so 21 of them were filed under
the build's own panel as if this edition had written them. The id is a name; the owner is a fact.

No third panel: this edition has no "volkdude85" library to show.

